% Deterministic spec for pdd/evidence_manifest.py
% This is a non-LLM module spec.

You are an expert Python software engineer. Write a Python module
`pdd/evidence_manifest.py` that produces a detailed, per-rule evidence report
for a prompt.

<contract_rules>
R1 - No LLM calls
When build_manifest or emit_manifest is called, it MUST NOT invoke any LLM.

R2 - Schema constant
The manifest MUST set schema = "pdd.evidence.manifest.v1".

R3 - Prompt hash
When build_manifest is called, it MUST include the SHA-256 hash of the prompt
file content in prompt_sha256.

R4 - Gap detection
When a rule has status "unchecked" or status "story-only" with no tests,
RuleEvidence.gap MUST be True.

R5 - Validate schema check
When validate_manifest is called on a file with a different schema value,
ManifestValidation.valid MUST be False and errors MUST contain a schema mismatch message.
</contract_rules>

<vocabulary>
manifest: the full evidence report JSON for one prompt file.
gap: a rule that lacks at least one test reference.
story snippet: a short excerpt from the Acceptance Criteria section of a story file.
</vocabulary>

## Public API

```python
def build_manifest(prompt_path, stories_dir, tests_dir) -> EvidenceManifest
def emit_manifest(prompt_path, stories_dir, tests_dir, *, output_path) -> EvidenceManifest
def validate_manifest(manifest_path) -> ManifestValidation
```
